{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/44426-wolf-and-rat","id":44426,"title":"Wolf and Rat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-07T14:11:26-08:00","id":44426,"title":"Wolf and Rat","content":"The orphanage stank of rot: rotten wood, rotten flesh. An odor so foul the pack didn't even need lupine senses to smell it. The place looked rundown, paint flaking away on the sign outside, the building itself seeming to sag like the shoulders of a sick man.<br /> <br /> Joseph Silver-Scar, their Rahu, sniffed in disgust. &quot;We should burn this whole place down. This sickness can't be cured.&quot; Joe never was very understanding of humans; he'd drifted further from humanity with each hunt, each passing year. Laughing-Mad, the Cahalith, elbowed him. She was the only one who could get away with it and not lose a limb or three. &quot;Bullshit,&quot; she said. &quot;That's our job. Don't be cruel.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's cruel to let these kids live. What is their lot? Lambs, weak, sick, forced to live to be eaten slowly by this ugly world.&quot;<br /> <br /> No-Moon's-Song exited the building and rejoined her pack across the street. &quot;We're all in. Told them we're here to check the mold in the basement. But ... I don't think they really care.&quot; She chewed her lip. &quot;They don't look much better than the kids. The whole place is diseased. The trail definitely ends here.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Or begins,&quot; said Joe. &quot;Either way, we're going to kill them all.&quot; He started across the street and the rest of the pack followed. Laughing-Mad fervently hoped he'd just meant the Beshilu.<br /> <div align=\"center\">* * *</div> They had to kick aside ratty old stuffed animals, broken toys and broken-spined books to move through the basement. What few patches of carpet remained were threadbare and stained. Across the basement room, upon a water-stained wall, No-Moon had drawn a large black X on the wall. &quot;That's the one. They're under there. You can hear 'em.&quot;<br /> <br /> The pack held their breath for a moment, straining to listen. There, behind the walls, a scrabbling sound, hundreds of nasty little rats scurrying. &quot;Rats,&quot; growled Joe. &quot;I fucking hate rats. City's full of 'em. I hate this city.&quot; Vermin alone weren't the issue; the <i>type </i>of rats were the problem. Gnawers, preying on the weak, spreading filth, chewing away at the <i>Zathu </i>until the spirits of pestilence flooded through and tainted the streets.<br /> <br /> Their Ithaeur, Amari Calls-the-Sun, spoke up for the first time. &quot;I can <i>feel </i>them.&quot; She grimaced. &quot;It makes me sick.&quot;<br /> <br /> Joseph's body swelled into the Dalu form. &quot;Then let's get this done. Nasty little bastards.&quot; His voice dropped to a deep growl.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shh!&quot; No-Moon's-Song held up a hand. &quot;You hear that? Nothing.&quot; The scrabbling in the walls had gone silent. &quot;They're waiting for us,&quot; she whispered.<br /> <br /> The pack tensed, two of them adopting the monstrous Urshul form, lupine muscles knotting in preparation for battle. Amari alone remained in Dalu, as Joseph grew even larger, Rage radiating from him like heat as he took Gauru and tore open the wall.<br /> <br /> Hundreds of rats flooded outward, swarming over the werewolves and into the room. Even as their filthy bodies broke apart to lupine claws and fangs, more came, a reek of tumorous death oozing out from the rent wall.<br /> <br /> Deep in the sewage-encrusted tunnels below, a blind rat looked upon the still-warm entrails of a sanitation worker splayed out before it. What it saw with dead, suppurating eyes only drove the rat swarm into a greater frenzy.<br /> <br /> For every rat that died, ten more boiled up out of the noxious dark.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:03:58-08:00","id":44504,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cCome. Hear. Lisssen.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It was Man that built the Wall. He builds it still. It freezes, it bites, it suffocates. What do you feel? There is nothing: no smell, no taste, no warmth. All is empty, all is fear. Wrong. Bad. It is his cage. Man didn't like the World That Was: nothing slept, had a will, had needs, fought back. He couldn't change it. Man wanted: wanted rule, wanted change. Nothing let him. So he built the Wall. Did it with Dreams. In Dreams, spirit goes Outside, shows itself. Man learns this, sees this. So he builds the Wall, and waits until we are sleeping. All things. When they dream, he pushes them to the far side, and seals it behind them. Now only Man and sleeping world here, and he can change it all he wants.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Only fear is here. Fear because of the Wolf. We once had purpose, had meaning. Chosen by Mother. Wolf is hate. Doesn't like us. Only likes to eat. Everything runs, everything prey, hates the brave. We Were not prey; we Were king, like Wolf was. Shaped the world. Hates us for it. If he is the Hunter, he can hunt king, and when all the world yelled \u201cno\u201d, he tore us to pieces. Makes fears. Proves a point: he hunts everything. Tore us to pieces, into little shreds, and then the Wall! Trapped we are, ruined we are. Hollow. Once had purpose, once shaped world. Now we are empty. And afraid.\u201d</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}